cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  ngs-germline-wes: a reproducible germline whole-exome variant calling pipeline
message: If you use this pipeline in your work, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: ver8ung
repository-code: https://github.com/ver8ung/germline-wes-pipeline
abstract: >-
  Germline short-variant calling from raw paired-end FASTQ to annotated VCF,
  following GATK best practices on GRCh38. Orchestrated with Snakemake, with
  every tool pinned in its own conda environment and the whole toolchain baked
  into a single Docker image so runs reproduce across Windows, macOS, Linux and
  HPC. Includes switchable exome capture-kit target sets and hap.py benchmarking
  against Genome in a Bottle truth sets.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - variant-calling
  - whole-exome-sequencing
  - GATK
  - snakemake
  - GRCh38
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
